quran[28]{c,v,t}:
  26,84,And bless me with an honourable reputation among the later generations.
  26,85,And place me among the heirs of the Garden of Bliss.
  26,86,"Forgive my (foster) father, for he is from those who have gone astray."
  26,87,"Do not disgrace me on the Day all will be resurrected,"
  26,88,"the Day when neither wealth nor children will benefit (any person),"
  26,89,except for him who appears before Allah with a sound heart.’
  26,90,"And Paradise will be brought near the God-conscious,"
  26,91,and the Hellfire will be displayed to the deviant.
  26,92,"Then, they shall be told: ‘Where are those (idols) you used to worship,"
  26,93,besides Allah. Are they helping you or helping each other?’
  26,94,"Then they shall be toppled into it—they (the idols) and the deviant (people),"
  26,95,and the troops of Iblis altogether.
  26,96,"There, they will say, disputing (with their idols):"
  26,97,"‘By Allah, indeed we were in manifest error,"
  26,98,when we made you equal with the Lord of all worlds.
  26,99,None caused us to go astray but the guilty.
  26,100,"So now we have no intercessors,"
  26,101,nor any sympathetic friend.
  26,102,"If we could return (to the world) once again, we would be among the believers.’"
  26,103,"There is indeed a sign in that, but most of them were not believers."
  26,104,"And indeed, your Lord is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
  26,105,The people of Nuh (Noah) rejected the messengers.
  26,106,When their (kinship) brother Nuh (Noah) said to them: ‘Will you not be God-conscious?
  26,107,"Indeed, I am a trustworthy messenger (sent) to you."
  26,108,So be God-conscious and obey me.
  26,109,I do not ask you for any reward for this (message). My reward lies only with the Lord of all worlds.
  26,110,So be God-conscious and obey me.’
  26,111,They said: ‘Shall we believe in you while the lowest people (of our society) follow you?’
